(obligation (id "OB-GC-COMPOSITION") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The profile's instruction set is RV64I plus the extensions M, A, F, D and C, plus Zicsr and Zifencei, plus Zicntr: 'G' is the defined abbreviation for the IMAFDZicsr_Zifencei base-and-extensions combination, and this profile is G plus C and Zicntr on the unprivileged side and Sstc on the privileged side.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-NAMING") (locator "36.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-ZICNTR") (locator "6.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SSTC") (locator "12.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-GC-COMPOSITION"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-GC-COMPOSITION"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-GC-COMPOSITION") (required_checks "CHK-GC-COMPOSITION-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-COMPOSITION-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-EXT-CLOSURE") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The extension dependency closure is complete under the pinned revision: D depends on F; F depends on Zicsr for control and status register access; and C decomposes as Zca always plus Zcd when D is present (Zcf exists only at RV32). Nothing in this profile is inferred from the letter 'G' alone.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-D") (locator "21.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-F") (locator "20.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-ZC") (locator "28.1.2")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-NAMING") (locator "36.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-EXT-CLOSURE"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-EXT-CLOSURE"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-EXT-CLOSURE") (required_checks "CHK-EXT-CLOSURE-POS") (required_checks "CHK-EXT-CLOSURE-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-PRIV-REVISION") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The privileged architecture is the pinned publication's: Machine-Level ISA Version 1.13 and Supervisor-Level ISA Version 1.13, under spec revision v20260120 — the same publication family as the unprivileged pin.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "11.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-PRIV-REVISION"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-PRIV-REVISION"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-PRIV-REVISION") (required_checks "CHK-PRIV-REVISION-POS") (required_checks "CHK-PRIV-REVISION-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-PRIV-MODES") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The profile implements machine, supervisor and user modes — the minimum a Linux-capable profile needs (M-mode firmware, S-mode kernel, U-mode userspace); the hypervisor extension is excluded, and every mode-dependent behaviour is tested in each supported mode (P4-SYSTEM.2).") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-INTRO") (locator "Introduction")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-PRIV-MODES"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-PRIV-MODES"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-PRIV-MODES") (required_checks "CHK-PRIV-MODES-POS") (required_checks "CHK-PRIV-MODES-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-SV39") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "Translation is Sv39: of the three paged virtual-memory schemes defined for SXLEN=64 (Sv39, Sv48, Sv57), the profile selects the minimal Linux-capable one — also the one the pinned SoC precedent implements (the FU540-C000's U54 supports Bare and Sv39). The U54's A/D behaviour (page faults instead of setting PTE A/D bits) is recorded as P4-SYSTEM.3's policy input, not as this profile's rule.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "§11.1.3–§11.1.4")) (source_refs (source_id "SIFIVE-FU540-C000") (locator "§4.7")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-SV39"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-SV39"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-SV39") (required_checks "CHK-SV39-POS") (required_checks "CHK-SV39-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-IALIGN-16") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "With the C extension present, IALIGN is 16 — instructions start on any 16-bit boundary — while ILEN remains 32; no instruction-address-misaligned exception arises from C's 16-bit forms.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-C") (locator "27.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-IALIGN-16"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-IALIGN-16"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-IALIGN-16") (required_checks "CHK-IALIGN-16-POS") (required_checks "CHK-IALIGN-16-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-ZICNTR") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The Zicntr base counters (cycle, time, instret) are included — explicitly beyond the G abbreviation — because a Linux-capable profile must offer the supervisor-mode time read; the counters' rate and progress semantics are the environment contract's to declare (P4-SYSTEM.5 and P4-SYSTEM.9), not this resolution's. Zihpm (hardware performance monitors) is not selected.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-ZICNTR") (locator "6.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-ZICNTR"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-ZICNTR"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-ZICNTR") (required_checks "CHK-ZICNTR-POS") (required_checks "CHK-ZICNTR-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-SSTC") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "Sstc is included — the supervisor timer-compare register stimecmp, gated by menvcfg.STCE — so an S-mode kernel programs its own timer without an M-mode round trip.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SSTC") (locator "12.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-SSTC"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-SSTC"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-SSTC") (required_checks "CHK-SSTC-POS") (required_checks "CHK-SSTC-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-FP-DEFER") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "F and D are in the profile because the standard RV64G userspace ABI is LP64D, which requires the D extension; the model implements no floating point until the floating-point backend passes qualification (P4-SYSTEM.7), the CPU-SYSTEM gate verdict reads incomplete until then, and a Sail-versus-Spike floating-point comparison is one implementation twice (the SoftFloat shared ancestry), never independent numeric evidence.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-PSABI") (locator "§2.4–§2.5")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-FP-DEFER"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-FP-DEFER"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-FP-DEFER") (required_checks "CHK-FP-DEFER-POS") (required_checks "CHK-FP-DEFER-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-ABI") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The toolchain ABI is LP64D — the standard RV64G ABI (ELFCLASS64 with EF_RISCV_FLOAT_ABI_DOUBLE, the hardware floating-point calling convention with ABI_FLEN=64); the toolchain is the host's clang/lld 21.1.8 with an rv64gc target (the existing guest-toolchain decision).") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-PSABI") (locator "§2.4–§2.5")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-ABI"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-ABI"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-ABI") (required_checks "CHK-ABI-POS") (required_checks "CHK-ABI-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-SBI") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The firmware contract for the Linux boot route is SBI 2.0: compatible M-mode firmware provides selected SBI services (timer, console, system reset, hart state management) before entering the S-mode kernel — real firmware, and a host-modelled SBI is a different contract, never silently substituted.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-SBI") (locator "Chapters 4–12")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-SBI"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-SBI"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-SBI") (required_checks "CHK-SBI-POS") (required_checks "CHK-SBI-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-CSR-SET") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The implemented CSR set is the committed minimum of 33: mhartid and misa; mstatus, mtvec, medeleg, mideleg, mie, mip, mscratch, mepc, mcause and mtval; menvcfg, mcounteren, mcycle and minstret; sstatus, stvec, sscratch, sepc, scause, stval, sie, sip and scounteren; satp; stimecmp; cycle, time and instret; and fflags, frm and fcsr. Per-CSR field semantics (WPRI/WARL/WLRL) belong to the privilege leaf (P4-SYSTEM.2).") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "11.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-CSR") (locator "1.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-F") (locator "20.1.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-ZICNTR") (locator "6.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SSTC") (locator "12.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-CSR-SET"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-CSR-SET"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-CSR-SET") (required_checks "CHK-CSR-SET-POS") (required_checks "CHK-CSR-SET-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-NO-PMP") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "PMP is excluded at v0: the privileged architecture's physical memory protection unit is optional, and the first boot contract does not require it; the decision is revisited by the board branch that needs it.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "§2.1.7")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-NO-PMP"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-NO-PMP"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-NO-PMP") (required_checks "CHK-NO-PMP-POS") (required_checks "CHK-NO-PMP-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-NO-H") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The hypervisor extension is excluded: the profile has one hart and no virtualization workload in the first Linux profile; H would arrive with a consumer, never ahead of one.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-INTRO") (locator "Introduction")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-NO-H"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-NO-H"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-NO-H") (required_checks "CHK-NO-H-POS") (required_checks "CHK-NO-H-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-RVWMO") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The memory consistency model is RVWMO: with the A extension in the profile the memory model is load-bearing even at one hart (the AMOs and their aq/rl annotations), and the multicore exposure of the weak model is MC-MULTICORE's, never smuggled in.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RVWMO") (locator "17.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-A") (locator "12.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-RVWMO"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-RVWMO"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-RVWMO") (required_checks "CHK-RVWMO-POS") (required_checks "CHK-RVWMO-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-PRIV-INSNS") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The privileged instructions in scope are mret, sret, wfi and sfence.vma (the pinned privileged instruction listings); wfi's wake semantics belong to the interrupt/counter/wait leaf (P4-SYSTEM.5).") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-INSNS") (locator "18.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "11.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-PRIV-INSNS"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-PRIV-INSNS"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-PRIV-INSNS") (required_checks "CHK-PRIV-INSNS-POS") (required_checks "CHK-PRIV-INSNS-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-RESOLUTION-ROUTE") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "This unit is a profile resolution: the selection is exact and citable, and the definition pipeline (encoding fragments, semantics, guests) has not started; the dossier declares the profile-resolution vehicle route, and the definition-pipeline gates refuse any encoding, state-census or guest-corpus document beside the declaration.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-INTRO") (locator "RISC-V Software Execution Environments and Harts")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-RESOLUTION-ROUTE"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-RESOLUTION-ROUTE"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-RESOLUTION-ROUTE") (required_checks "CHK-RESOLUTION-ROUTE-POS") (required_checks "CHK-RESOLUTION-ROUTE-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-SCOPE-CENSUS") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The scope block enumerates the RV64I base census (52 forms — the same enumeration and source as rv64i-lab-v0); each extension's instruction census lands with its encoding fragment in the evidence leaves (the RV32/64G listings and the privileged listings are the census references), and the declared scope grows only with them.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.4–§1.1.8")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV64I") (locator "§3.1.2–§3.1.3")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-G-LISTING") (locator "35.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-INSNS") (locator "18.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-SCOPE-CENSUS"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-SCOPE-CENSUS"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-SCOPE-CENSUS") (required_checks "CHK-SCOPE-CENSUS-POS") (required_checks "CHK-SCOPE-CENSUS-NEG"))
